{"v":3,"topic":"sub:11|Formulas and equations|Change the subject","q":{"7777":{"stem":null,"options":[{"label":"A","latex":"$y = \\dfrac{2x+6}{3}$","is_correct":0,"key_source":"extracted","fig":null},{"label":"B","latex":"$y = \\dfrac{2x-6}{3}$","is_correct":1,"key_source":"extracted","fig":null},{"label":"C","latex":"$y = \\dfrac{2}{3}x - 6$","is_correct":0,"key_source":"extracted","fig":null},{"label":"D","latex":"$y = \\dfrac{2}{3}x + 6$","is_correct":0,"key_source":"extracted","fig":null}],"opt_table":null,"layout":"text","figures":[],"parts":[{"id":12371,"latex":"Which of the equations below, correctly expresses $y$ as the subject for the following formula:\n\n$$2x - 3y = 6$$","needs_review":0,"c17":null,"note":null,"can_use":[]}],"solutions":[{"id":11862,"part_id":null,"source":"extracted","latex":"$$\\begin{aligned} 2x - 3y &= 6 \\\\ -3y &= 6 - 2x \\\\ y &= \\dfrac{2x - 6}{3} \\end{aligned}$$\nThis matches option B.","criteria":[[1,"Correct answer"]],"meta":{"format_note":"Rubric row added for MCQ."}}]},"7922":{"stem":null,"options":[],"opt_table":null,"layout":null,"figures":[],"parts":[{"id":12587,"latex":"Given $v = u + at$ rearrange the equation so that $a$ is the subject.","needs_review":0,"c17":null,"note":null,"can_use":[]}],"solutions":[{"id":12040,"part_id":null,"source":"extracted","latex":"$$\\begin{aligned} v &= u + at \\\\ v - u &= at &&(\\text{subtract } u) \\\\ \\dfrac{v - u}{t} &= a &&(\\text{divide by } t) \\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\therefore\\ a = \\dfrac{v - u}{t}$$","criteria":[[2,"Correct answer"],[1,"Makes one correct step in rearranging, or equivalent merit"]],"meta":{"format_note":"Rubric written by us."}}]}}}